    "created_at": "2021-02-16T15:59:06Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-16T15:59:06Z",
    "body": "I totally agree that the goal request generally will be in the same frame as the costmap. My point was just that that is not what the interface suggests and that a goal request in another frame should be fine as long as its transformable in this frame and the results lies within costmap boundaries.\r\n\r\nI can think of some cases where a goal in a different frame might be beneficial.\r\nFor example in my case there is a static transform `world`->`map` to align a graph map recorded with `slam_toolbox` with a global origin. Goals are generally given with respect to this global origin not the actual map frame.\r\n\r\nSuch a check/transformation could be implemented at two different levels, namely in `PlannerServer::computePlan` (https://github.com/ros-planning/navigation2/blob/main/nav2_planner/src/planner_server.cpp#L209) or in the implementation of `createPlan` of the respective planner plugin (https://github.com/ros-planning/navigation2/blob/main/nav2_navfn_planner/src/navfn_planner.cpp#L118).\r\n\r\nIs this a feature you would like to see implemented, and if so, would you prefer is at a planner server or planner plugin level?\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
